      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a decent start on the technical side, but it's a bit of a wall of text. It doesn't feel \"Nature Physics\" level yet—it needs more formal structure to separate the different points of contention. \n\nCan you expand this? I need you to break down the critique into specific technical categories (e.g., the modeling error, the noise implications, the theoretical inconsistency) to make it easier for a reader to scan. Just remember: keep it substantive. I see the score on my end is still pretty low because there aren't enough sections, but don't just give me a bunch of headers with one sentence under each. Make the sections actually meaningful.",
